      'Quoted lines are from the 2006 Destiny Image edition of Kingdom Principles, cited by page; spacing around punctuation has been normalized and the list number before the p. 87 line dropped. The book’s twelve chapters run from The Priority of the Kingdom, The Kingdom of God Versus the Governments of Man and The Original Kingdom Concept: Colonization of Earth through nine Kingdom Concepts in turn: Kings, Lord, Territory, Constitution, Law, Keys, Citizenship, Culture, and Giving to the King. The line about a destructive ideology sustained and validated by a theology is printed in quotation marks in the 2013 Destiny Image edition itself, beside the publisher’s web address, and the publisher’s description quotes it as his. His Brazil illustration, of a son who "was sovereign in Brazil but ruled as a regent under his father, the king of the Portuguese empire", is a teaching picture of delegated rule. His statement that in the Kingdom of Heaven there are no shortages is his; the lesson weighs it against the Word, which shows believers in this age sometimes in real need and the Kingdom answering need through Yahweh’s supply and the sharing of His people.',
